message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Thermodynamic Profiling for Synonymous Variant Classification"
authors:
  - family-names: "Vilar-Sanchez"
    given-names: "Jose Antonio"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-1057-4223"
    affiliation: "Universitat Oberta de Catalunya"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-05-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/josevilar-qbioai/synonymous-thermodynamic-classification"
keywords:
  - synonymous variants
  - thermodynamic profiling
  - stacking free energy
  - deep learning
  - variant classification
  - ClinVar
  - bioinformatics
abstract: >-
  A 1D convolutional neural network that classifies pathogenic synonymous
  variants using nearest-neighbor stacking free energy profiles. Achieves
  AUC 0.683 on 5-fold CV and demonstrates universal transferability via
  Leave-One-Gene-Out validation (AUC 0.625, 72% of genes above chance).
